#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/grdinfo.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.grdinfo.grdinfo:79
msgid ""
"[*dz*]\\ [**+a**\\ [*alpha*]]\\ [**+s**]. Determine minimum and maximum z-"
"values. If *dz* is provided then we first round these values off to "
"multiples of *dz*. To exclude the two tails of the distribution when "
"determining the minimum and maximum you can add **+a** to set the *alpha* "
"value (in percent): We then sort the grid, exclude the data in the 0.5*\\ "
"*alpha* and 100 - 0.5*\\ *alpha* tails, and revise the minimum and maximum. "
"To force a symmetrical range about zero, using minus/plus the maximum "
"absolute value of the two extremes, append **+s**. We report the result via "
"the text string *zmin/zmax* or *zmin/zmax/dz* (if *dz* was given) as "
"expected by :func:`pygmt.makecpt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/grdinfo.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.grdinfo.grdinfo:91
msgid ""
"*xmin/xmax/ymin/ymax*\\ [**+r**][**+u**\\ *unit*]. Specify the :doc:`region "
"</tutorials/basics/regions>` of interest."
msgstr ""

